---
title: Pumpkin Chocolate Chip Muffins
image: https://butternutbakeryblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/moist-pumpkin-muffin-225x225.jpg
course: Dessert
cuisine: American
source: https://butternutbakeryblog.com/pumpkin-chocolate-chip-muffins/
prep time: 20 minutes
servings: 12
author: Jenna Barnard
cook time: 30 minutes
time required: 50 minutes
---

Preheat the oven to 350*F.

Lightly grease the surface of a #muffin tin{}, not inside the cavities, but just around the top rim of each. Fill with 12 paper liners.

In a #large mixing bowl{}, whisk together @pumpkin puree{1%15oz can}(i.e. Libby’s), @granulated sugar{1%cup}, @light brown sugar{1/2%cup}(packed), @vegetable oil{1/2%cup}, @eggs{2%large}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, and @sour cream{1/4%cup}.

Once smooth, whisk in @baking powder{1%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, @?pumpkin pie spice{1.25%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp}.

Add in @all purpose flour{2%cups} and whisk until it's about halfway incorporated. 

Dump in @semisweet chocolate chips{3/4%cups} and use a rubber spatula to fold and fully combine the batter.

Divide the batter between the 12 liners, filling each all the way to the top and then some.

Top each muffin with a tiny handful of extra @?semisweet chocolate chips{}.

Bake for ~{25-30%minutes} or until a toothpick in the center comes out clean with a few moist crumbs.

Allow the muffins to rest for ~{5%minutes}, then carefully release and transfer to a cooling rack.